# Pairs with RoutingConverges. Reproduces the liveness half of #4452 under the
# spec's own fairness: a split commits on T while a resize is in flight, then
# the resize is undone. The undo restores the map captured when the resize
# began, which still routes k2 to s1, while T/s1 keeps the split's moved-away
# fence, so the registry's own pair is refused for k2 forever.
#
# DEADLOCK: off for the same reason as UniqueOwnerSplitDuringResize.
MODULE: RoutingConvergesUndoAfterSplit
TARGET: RoutingConverges
CLASS: Temporal
DEADLOCK: off
SUMMARY: an undo after a split that committed during the resize restores a map the old copy refuses forever
PERTURBS: ResizeBegin

--- FIND
    /\ rs # "migrating"
    /\ sp \in {"idle", "done"}
    /\ rz' = "snap"
--- REPLACE
    /\ rs # "migrating"
\* MUTATION: no interlock with an in-flight split.
    /\ rz' = "snap"
--- END